  "sources": [
    {
      "url": "https://orbbec-debian-repos-aws.s3.amazonaws.com/product/Gemini%20330%20series%20Datasheet-V1.8.pdf",
      "title": "Gemini 330 Series Datasheet for USB Devices (revision history to V1.8; pages headed V1.7), Orbbec",
      "read": "2026-11-07",
      "covers": "specification table (section 2), dimensions and weight (Table 3-2-3), LDM, IR and RGB module tables (3-4-3 to 3-4-5), USB 3.0 stream table (4-4-3), typical depth intrinsics (4-5-2), stream FOVs (4-5-3), minimum-Z (4-6-1), coordinate system positions (4-8-1, 4-8-4), start points (4-9-1), depth performance (5-1-1), power (5-1-1/5-1-2 of section 5.2)"
    }
  ],
  "note": "The long-baseline (95 mm) Gemini 330, in an IP65 housing, with a global-shutter RGB camera. Poses: the depth origin is the left IR module's optical centre (section 4.8); the right IR one stated baseline along -y; the colour origin is \"X 23.75, Y 0, Z 0\" mm from the depth origin (Table 4-8-1; Table 4-8-4 puts depth and colour at X 0 and 23.75 mm, the same Z), entered as body (0, -23.75, 0) mm with pose_stated true, axes taken parallel (no rotation stated). The projector (LDM, 850 nm VCSEL, 101 x 72.5 deg) is drawn between the IR modules but its offset is not dimensioned in the text: placed at the baseline midpoint as an ASSUMPTION (pose_stated false). FOVs: the IR stream FOVs of Table 4-5-3 (91 x 65 deg for 16:10, 91 x 60 for 16:9, 81 x 65 for 4:3, 91 x 14 for 848 x 100; the IR modules are 94/68/104 deg, Table 3-4-4); depth FOV before D2C 90 x 65 deg at 2 m; RGB 94 x 68 deg (16:10), 94 x 62 (16:9), 82 x 68 (4:3). Typical depth intrinsics fx = fy = 620.0 px at 1280 x 800 (Table 4-5-2, shared by the series). min_z is Table 4-6-1 at a disparity search range of 128 (0.5 m at the 16:10 modes and 1280 x 720; with 64, 1 m); the specification table instead gives \"0.25m @ 1280 x 800 / 1280 x 720 / 640 x 400 / 424 x 266\", which matches no 335L/336L column of Table 4-6-1, and the power tables' typical configuration uses a search range of 256, whose min-Z is not tabulated; the 4:3 and 848 x 100 rows are not given for the L models. Streams: Table 4-4-3 (USB 3.0); depth Y16, IR Y8, colour MJPEG or YUYV (YUYV entered, 16 bits per pixel by the 4:2:2 definition). Power: average < 3.0 W (entered), peak < 6.0 W. The lens model pinhole is a labelled ASSUMPTION (distortion < 1.5%, no coefficients). Not stated: pixel size, f-numbers, subpixel accuracy. Mounting: bottom 1x 1/4-20 UNC, back 2x M4. Gemini 336L: the 335L with an IR-pass filter cover (section 3.4.7); size 124 x 29 x 27.7 mm, 135 g; depth and RGB start points 4.780 mm behind the front cover glass (Table 4-9-1).",
  "interface": "USB 3.0 (USB Type-C)",
